            <ArticleTitle>Pneumatosis cystoides intestinalis. Presentation as an acute abdomen.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>571-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>It is rare for pneumatosis cystoides intestinalis to give rise to abdominal pain. We report a patient with signs and symptoms of a perforated viscous in whom abdominal exploration was negative, but in whom biopsy of various intraabdominal cystic structures revealed only pneumatosis cystoides intestinalis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
